        "Content": "16 Westpoint Manor, Quigleys Point, Co. Donegal F93 W983\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 28th of October 2026. \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Coastal Location \r\n\r\nLocation Quigleys Point, Moville 13km, Derry 12m, Burnfoot 17km, Letterkenny 45km, \r\n\r\nThe property is located within the Westpoint Manor estate, in the coastal village Quigleys Point. Population (2022) 213. It is a village in Co Donegal. Located on the eastern shores of Inishowen and overlooking Lough Foyle, the village is sometimes known locally as \"Carrowkeel\". To the south is the city of Derry and to the north lie the villages of Moville and Greencastle. A car ferry links Greencastle with Magilligan during the summer. The village has a school, shop, pub, fish & chip shop, A local community centre & health centre and sporting clubs. Larger towns, with further amenities are a short drive. Nearby beaches include Sweet Nellie's Beach (Greencastle), Culdaff Beach, and Stroove Beach / Big White Bay. \r\n\r\nDescription DL47964F\r\n\r\nThe subject property is a two-story semi-detached dwelling house believed to date from 2001, contained within a mature development. The 113.15 sq.mt 1,218 sq. ft of accommodation comprises of a hall, sitting room, kitchen, utility room, and WC, 4 bedrooms one ensuite and a family bathroom. There is parking to the front. There is the added benefit on an enclosed rear garden with side access. The property sits on an elevated site with rear views of the sea and a short walk to the village. \r\n\r\nThe property is occupied under terms unknown. \r\n\r\nBER C3 #107838260\r\n\r\nViewing - By appointment \r\n\r\nSolicitors Eoin Pentony, Healy Pentony, 12 Merrion Square North, Dublin 2,\r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
      },
